.TH AVR-UPDI-GDB 1 "2026-05-17" "avr-updi-gdb 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
avr-updi-gdb \- UPDI-to-GDB debug stub with avrOS FSM awareness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr-updi-gdb
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-baud
.IR baud ]
.RB [ \-\-load ]
.I serial-device
.I elf-file
.br
.B avr-updi-gdb
.B \-\-device
.RB [ \-\-baud
.IR baud ]
.I serial-device
.RI [ elf-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B avr-updi-gdb
is a host-side GDB Remote Serial Protocol (RSP) server that bridges
.BR avr-gdb (1)
to AVR DA/DB targets over the UPDI single-wire debug interface.
It exposes each cooperative FSM task registered with the avrOS
runtime as a GDB virtual thread, so standard
.B info threads
and per-thread breakpoints work against an RTOS-aware view of the
target.
.PP
The server reads symbols and avrOS sentinel-table addresses from
.IR elf-file ,
opens
.I serial-device
as the UPDI UART, and listens on a TCP port for a single
.BR avr-gdb (1)
client. All UPDI memory access is non-intrusive when the CPU is
halted by GDB; no heap allocation occurs on the hot path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
TCP port to listen on for the
.BR avr-gdb (1)
client. Must satisfy
.RI 1 " " \(<= " " port " " \(<= " " 65535 .
Defaults to
.BR 1234 .
.TP
.BI \-\-baud " baud"
UART baud rate to the UPDI adapter. Must be a positive integer
accepted by the host
.BR termios (3)
layer. Defaults to
.BR 115200 .
.TP
.B \-\-load
Before entering the event loop, program
.I elf-file
into target FLASH via the UPDI NVM controller. On any write failure
the process exits 1 without opening the GDB listener.
.TP
.B \-\-device
One-shot diagnostic. Open UPDI, read the SIGROW signature, revision,
serial number and ASI status registers, print a human-readable report
to standard output and exit. No TCP listener is opened, no ELF is
loaded, and the target CPU is not halted. Useful as a first-line check
for wiring, target power, and the UPDIDIS fuse. Mutually exclusive
with
.BR \-\-load .
The
.I elf-file
operand is optional in this mode.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I serial-device
Path to the USB-serial adapter
.RI ( /dev/ttyUSB0 ", " /dev/cu.usbserial-* ", \(or similar)").
.TP
.I elf-file
AVR ELF binary used for symbol lookup and avrOS table discovery.
With
.B \-\-load
this file is also written to FLASH.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown
.RB ( SIGINT ,
.BR SIGTERM ,
or GDB
.B k
kill packet).
.TP
.B 1
Bad arguments, serial-device open failure, TCP bind failure,
.B \-\-load
flash write failure, or
.B \-\-device
SIGROW read failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Attach to a running target without flashing:
.PP
.RS
.EX
avr-updi-gdb /dev/ttyUSB0 firmware.elf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Flash and debug from cold on a non-default port:
.PP
.RS
.EX
avr-updi-gdb \-\-load \-\-port 1234 \-\-baud 115200 \\
             /dev/ttyUSB0 firmware.elf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Once the server is listening, in another terminal:
.PP
.RS
.EX
avr-gdb firmware.elf
(gdb) target remote :1234
(gdb) info threads
(gdb) monitor avros events
.EE
.RE
.PP
Verify the UPDI link without starting a GDB listener:
.PP
.RS
.EX
avr-updi-gdb \-\-device /dev/ttyUSB0
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr-gdb (1),
.BR avrdude (1),
.BR termios (3)
